## Project Rules for agy-kit

### Planning First
- With any feature touching >3 files or changing architecture, create `plans/SPEC_<feature>.md` first.
- SPEC must include: use-cases, data flow, files to modify/create, API schema, edge-cases, backward compatibility.

### Test-Driven Development
- Every new logic must ship with Unit/Integration Test.
- Enforce RED → GREEN → REFACTOR cycle. Confirm test FAIL before writing logic.

### Quality Gates
- Linter & Typecheck: 0 error, 0 warning.
- Never hardcode secrets, API keys, or passwords.
- OWASP security scan mandatory before merge.

### Git Convention
- Group commits into complete feature units (Conventional Commits).
- Do NOT commit single files one by one.

### Workflow
[Plan] → [TDD] → [Quality Gate] → [E2E QA] → [Review & Commit]

### Rollback Safety
- Create git checkpoint before agent code changes.
- Auto-rollback on test failure.
- Max 3 retries per failing test, then escalate.
